  },
  "dynamics_and_shift_analysis": {
    "stability_of_coalitions": "Neither coalition shifted between Round 3 and Round 4. The 6 G proponents (Colleagues 1, 5, 7, 9, 13, 14) mounted a synchronized, chemically precise offensive focusing on the confounding presence of 7 mM sodium glutamate (35 mM carbon) in BM2 medium. However, the M faction (led by Colleagues 2, 3, 4, 10, 11, 12) held firm by leaning heavily on the 'literal wording' defense—arguing that Statement III does not state 'sole carbon source in the absence of amino acids' and that standard literature defines BM2-glycerol as having glycerol as the carbon source.",
    "analysis_of_M_anchors": {
      "Colleague 2 & Colleague 3": "Originally voted G in Round 0, but have now become the most vocal defenders of M, citing Köhler et al. (2000) and the biosynthetic pathways (GlpK/GlpD -> DHAP -> HAA and dTDP-L-rhamnose). They feel intellectually vindicated by having found the exact paper that refuted their initial gut instinct.",
